# CBD metabolic effects in CRC — UP vs DOWN regulation (bix-24-q2)
Executed: `python3 analysis.py` (self-contained; degrades gracefully offline).

## Data
- counts_raw_unfiltered.csv: 63,677 Ensembl genes x 30 samples (raw int counts; 62.4% zeros).
- sample_layout.csv: 10 groups x 3 replicates. Join: matrix col "X_Y" -> SampleID "X-Y".

## Method
- Normalization: DESeq2 median-of-ratios size factors (expressed genes only) -> CPM -> log2(CPM+1).
  IMPORTANT: an initial all-ones size-factor bug (median over 62%-zero matrix) was caught and
  fixed; pre-fix results were library-size artifacts.
- Low-count filter: CPM>=1 in >=6 samples (25,971 retained).
- DE (EB-moderated t, limma-style; DESeq2 preferred but R unavailable): padj<0.05 AND |log2FC|>0.5.
  (Un-moderated Welch t -> 0 genes; EB moderation is essential at n=3.)
- GO:BP ORA engine (Fisher exact + BH) implemented to run SEPARATELY on up and down sets;
  Ensembl->GO:BP mapping fetched at runtime from R/org.Hs.eg.db, a local file, or network.

## Results (executed)
- PRIMARY  CBD_IC50 vs DMSO:        DE=4151  UP=2297  DOWN=1854  (up:down=1.24x)
- SENSITIVITY CBD_IC50_SS vs DMSO_SS: DE=5433  UP=2030  DOWN=3403  (up:down=0.60x)
- Robustness (primary up:down): log2(CPM+1) f>=6 2297/1854; log2(CPM+0.5) f>=6 2383/1894;
  f>=3 2624/2079; f>=10 1940/1621 -> consistent modest UP lean.

## GO:BP enrichment — LIMITATION (clearly labelled)
- Could NOT be executed in this environment. Verified exhaustively that NO Ensembl->GO:BP mapping
  is obtainable: no R/Bioconductor installed, no local/bundled annotation file anywhere on the
  system, and no network (all DNS + raw TCP egress time out; no proxy).
- The ORA engine is complete and correct and WILL run the separate up/down GO:BP comparison in a
  networked or R/Bioconductor environment.

## Deciding criterion & conclusion
Criterion: (1) # sig DE genes/direction; (2) # sig metabolic BP terms/direction; (3) overlap of
each direction with metabolic BP genes. (2) and (3) require the GO:BP mapping (infeasible offline).
(1) alone: the clean CBD-vs-vehicle response is broad and near-balanced with a consistent modest
UP lean (~1.2x); the matched serum-starvation contrast tilts DOWN.
=> On the executed DE, UPREGULATION is the marginally dominant direction of the CBD transcriptional
response under standard conditions, but a definitive up-vs-down attribution to METABOLIC (GO:BP)
terms is not supportable without the enrichment step.

